powah.guide.charging=Use a Binding Card in the air to bind it to yourself. Put the card into a powered Player Transmitter to charge items in your inventory. Ordinary cards work in the same dimension.\nUse a Binding Card on an Enderman or Endermite to make a Dimensional Binding Card; the entity is consumed. Existing player binding is preserved.\nAn Energy Hopper charges items in the inventory on its facing side. It supports vanilla containers and Forge modifiable item handlers. An Energy Discharger draws power from up to seven items and outputs FE.\nSneak-use a Battery to enable automatic charging of carried items. Batteries never charge each other. Use an Aerial Pearl on a zombie to obtain a Player Aerial Pearl. Use a Photoelectric Pane on an Enderman or Endermite for a Lens of Ender.
powah.guide.charging.title=Charging Players and Items
powah.guide.ender=Ender Cells and Gates use a persistent network keyed by the placing player's UUID and the selected channel. Matching networks work across dimensions while their blocks are loaded.\nA new channel has zero capacity. Open an Ender Cell and Shift-click an Energy Cell or Battery in your inventory. It is consumed, adding its capacity and existing energy permanently to that channel. The two visible slots on the left charge items.\nSet an Ender Gate to the same channel. Power passes through its attached face. Different players and different channels remain isolated.\nHigher tiers unlock up to 12 channels. Breaking an Ender Cell does not remove the channel's energy or capacity. Only its owner or an operator can change its configuration.
powah.guide.ender.title=Ender Networks
powah.guide.energizing=Right-use an Energizing Orb to insert one ingredient. With an empty hand, retrieve an item; sneak-use to retrieve all. Pipes insert in slots 2-7 and extract from slot 1.\nPower an Energizing Rod at its attached face. It finds the nearest orb within four blocks. Multiple rods can supply one orb. Wrench link mode selects an orb, then a rod.\nIron + gold: 2 Energized Steel, 10,000 FE. Blaze rod or 4 blaze powder: Blazing Crystal, 120,000 FE. Diamond: Niotic Crystal, 300,000 FE. Emerald: Spirited Crystal, 1,000,000 FE.\nNether star + 2 redstone blocks + Blazing Crystal Block: 16 Nitro Crystals, 20,000,000 FE. Each ingredient needs its own slot. Extract the completed result before adding the next recipe.
powah.guide.energizing.title=Energizing
powah.guide.interaction_recipe=Use the interaction described on this page.
powah.guide.intro=Powah generates, stores and transmits Forge Energy (FE). Start by crafting Dielectric Paste from coal, clay and a lava bucket.\nProgress through Starter, Basic, Hardened, Blazing, Niotic, Spirited and Nitro tiers. Energizing unlocks the advanced materials.\nUse a Wrench in air to cycle rotation, side configuration and linking. Sneak-use a machine to dismantle it. Stored energy and fluids are preserved; inventory contents are returned.\nIf Ponder is installed, hover over a machine and hold W, or use the Ponder link. Scroll to read longer pages.
powah.guide.intro.title=Powah! Field Guide
powah.guide.materials=Uraninite has poor, regular and dense ores. Mine ores for Raw Uraninite, then smelt it, or energize it for double output. Energizing ore blocks yields 3, 5 or 10 Uraninite depending on richness.\nIn 1.12 terrain, poor ore generates at Y 4-63, regular ore at Y 4-23, and dense ore at Y 4-11. Dry Ice generates under cold biomes. Deepslate ores are available for custom worlds.\nBlue Ice is supplied as powah:blue_ice because 1.12 lacks it. Craft it from 9 packed ice; energize 2 Blue Ice with 10,000 FE to make Dry Ice.\nA Charged Snowball costs 500,000 FE and summons lightning on impact. Shared recipe ingredients use the Forge ore dictionary. Uranium ingots can be energized only when another mod supplies them.
powah.guide.materials.title=Resources and Legacy Changes
powah.guide.no_results=No matching pages.
powah.guide.ponder=Ponder
powah.guide.power=Furnator: insert furnace fuel in the fuel slot. One coal yields 48,000 FE by default. A full buffer pauses fuel use.\nMagmator: fill with lava using a bucket or fluid pipe. One bucket yields 100,000 FE.\nThermo Generator: supply water, and place lava, magma or a Blazing Crystal Block below it. Water use is 1 mB per 40 active ticks.\nSolar Panel: needs clear sky and daylight. An installed Lens of Ender bypasses obstructions. It still needs daylight.\nEnergy Cells store FE. Connect generators with Energy Cables; the slowest cable limits the path. Use side buttons to choose input, output or disabled. Both slots on the left of an Energy Cell charge items; Furnators, Magmators and Thermo Generators use their lower-left slot.
powah.guide.power.title=Generation and Storage
powah.guide.reactor=Carry 36 identical Reactor parts and place them in an empty 3 x 4 x 3 area. The clicked location is the bottom center. Placement consumes 36 parts.\nSlots: lower-left chargeable item; center Uraninite; upper-left furnace fuel; bottom-left redstone; bottom-right solid coolant. Fluid pipes and buckets supply water. Ice, snowballs, packed ice, Blue Ice and Dry Ice are solid coolants.\nThe reactor stores up to 1,000 fuel units; each Uraninite adds 100. Coal and redstone improve efficiency. Water and solid coolant reduce temperature and fuel consumption.\nConnect cables to the bottom center, four lower side centers or top center. Auto mode pauses at full storage and resumes at 70%.\nBreaking any part dismantles the structure and refunds 36 parts plus its inventory. Stored energy and fluid travel with the returned parts.
